                <h2>Applicable Scenarios and Prerequisites</h2>
<p>This SOP applies to operational teams running ads on mainstream overseas platforms such as Meta, Google, and TikTok. Audit frequency recommendation: mandatory check before ad launch, weekly routine audits, and special inspections before major campaigns. Operators should log into each platform backend in advance and verify account status and sufficient balance.</p>
<h2>Step 1: Account Basic Settings Check</h2>
<p>Before starting any campaigns, complete the following checklist:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Account Entity Information</strong>: Confirm business license and legal representative details match the account opening records. Ad account names must not contain sensitive terms (such as "official" or "authorized" exaggerated statements)</li>
<li><strong>Timezone and Currency</strong>: Ensure alignment with financial reconciliation cycles to avoid data discrepancies from timezone errors</li>
<li><strong>Payment Methods</strong>: Verify credit card or recharge account balance and set balance alerts in advance (recommend 1.5-2x daily average spend as buffer)</li>
<li><strong>User Permissions</strong>: Review the list of personnel with ad deployment access and promptly remove accounts of departed employees</li>
</ol>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Operator Tip</strong>: A certain e-commerce team experienced repeated reconciliation errors because their Google Ads timezone was set to UTC+8, causing an 8-hour discrepancy with their financial system, consuming significant manpower to verify.</p>
</blockquote>
<h2>Step 2: Ad Creative Compliance Review</h2>
<p>Creatives are the core audit area with varying standards across platforms:</p>
<p><strong>Universal Checkpoints (applicable to all platforms):</strong><br />
- Images/videos contain no nudity or excessive sexual suggestive elements<br />
- Text occupies no more than 20% of image area (some platforms are stricter)<br />
- No comparative claims (such as "world's first" or "best product" absolute statements)<br />
- Music/fonts used are licensed or in public domain</p>
<p><strong>Platform-Specific Items:</strong><br />
- Meta (Facebook/Instagram): Currency symbols should not appear directly in creatives; guide users to landing pages<br />
- Google Ads: Healthcare and financial products require additional qualification reviews; efficacy claims need data support<br />
- TikTok: Prioritize vertical videos; first 3 seconds must be eye-catching; avoid engagement-bait language</p>
<h2>Step 3: Audience Targeting and Data Usage Compliance</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Interest Targeting</strong>: Avoid interest words related to protected attributes (such as specific racial or religious groups)</li>
<li><strong>Custom Audiences</strong>: Before uploading customer data, confirm users have provided consent authorization, complying with GDPR, CCPA, and other data protection regulations</li>
<li><strong>Similar Audiences</strong>: Ensure seed data volume is sufficient (recommend 1000+ people) to avoid targeting failures from data quality issues</li>
<li><strong>Retargeting</strong>: Set reasonable silence periods (e.g., remove after 30 days of no interaction) to avoid repeatedly targeting already-purchased users</li>
</ol>
<h2>Step 4: Landing Page and Conversion Path Check</h2>
<p>Compliant creatives with non-compliant landing pages can still result in account restrictions:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>URL Security</strong>: Use HTTPS protocol and ensure domain is not on platform blacklists</li>
<li><strong>Content Consistency</strong>: Landing page product information, prices, and offers must match ad promises; avoid exaggerations</li>
<li><strong>Privacy Policy</strong>: Page footer must have an accessible privacy policy link with content compliant with target market regulations</li>
<li><strong>Payment Process</strong>: E-commerce landing pages require security certification badges (such as PCI DSS) on payment pages</li>
<li><strong>Loading Speed</strong>: Mobile first-screen loading should not exceed 3 seconds; test using Google PageSpeed Insights</li>
</ul>
<h2>Step 5: Financial and Recharge Compliance</h2>
<p>This most easily overlooked area has the biggest impact:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Budget Allocation</strong>: Daily ad budget should not exceed 150% of the account's daily average spend to avoid triggering risk controls from abnormal spending</li>
<li><strong>Recharge Records</strong>: Screenshot after each recharge to ensure the credited amount matches the actual amount</li>
<li><strong>Invoice Reconciliation</strong>: Monthly reconcile platform bills with actual spend and promptly appeal any discrepancies</li>
<li><strong>Multi-Account Management</strong>: Accounts under the same entity should maintain consistent spending patterns to avoid being flagged as suspicious from sudden large-scale spending</li>
</ol>
